{"key":"map/gz36j","relations":[{"id":"people","rows":[{"detail":"","key":"character/firez","title":"Firez","variant":""}],"title":"Inhabitants"},{"id":"inhabitant","rows":[{"detail":"","key":"creature/zonefinal%20jun%20firez%20m","title":"Firez","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"creature/zonefinal%20skeleton","title":"Golden skeleton","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"creature/zone35%20zombie%20m","title":"Soldier zombie (variant 6)","variant":""},{"detail":"","key":"creature/zone35%20zombie%20f","title":"Zombified warrior woman (variant 4)","variant":""}],"title":"Creatures and people"},{"id":"quest","rows":[{"detail":"","key":"quest/q22j","title":"Firez","variant":""}],"title":"Quests"}],"versions":[{"guide":"","html":"<article><h1>Throne room</h1><p>The mad necromancer Firez uses this hall as both throne room and treasury. The final battle with him will decide Jigran's fate.</p><h2>Firez’s identity and the final confrontation</h2><p>In the throne room, Firez reveals that he too is a Joon and has watched Kir through a dragonet since the escape. He says his people expelled him for necromancy and claims that his rule protected them from the Curse. Kir answers with their enslavement, his parents’ deaths and the destruction of Jigran to prolong Firez’s life. The tyrant’s explanation is his own defence, not proof that the captivity was benevolent. He threatens to kill Kir, raise him as an obedient servant and use him against the baron. Their exchange leads into the final battle for Jigran. [1, 2]</p><h2>Sources</h2><p>Based on the original dialogue, quest journals and world descriptions. Source numbers identify the evidence listed below.</p><table data-columns=\"2\"><tr><th>#</th><th>Sources</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Dialogue · <a href=\"wiki://character/hero\">Kir</a>, <a href=\"wiki://character/firez\">Firez</a> (briefing brief_349)</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>World description · Throne room (zone gz36j)</td></tr></table><table data-columns=\"2\"><tr><th>Property</t